IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcin-common`
IMPORT `wcin-dates`
IMPORT `wcin-wirc-2013`
IMPORT `wcin-aca-1985`

-- Victorian workers' compensation indexation notice, Gazette S 363 of 30 June 2026 -- the injured worker's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the injured worker, with a claim under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 or, for an
-- older claim, under the Accident Compensation Act 1985. "What is the most I can be paid each week? What are my weekly
-- payments after the maximum? What deemed earnings apply to me? What does the notice print for my impairment rating, and
-- what is my lump sum after the maximum? What does the no-disadvantage table give? What are the damages thresholds and
-- maxima?" The facts are ones the worker can state, or read from the insurer's decision: the Act the claim is under, the
-- relevant day, the entitlement period, the impairment rating, and the amounts the Act's own formulas give (the Acts are not
-- deposited, so those formulas are inputs). The rules are in wcin-wirc-2013.l4 and wcin-aca-1985.l4; this module restates
-- none. Its names differ from wcin-seat-family.l4's, so a case file can import both.
--
-- WHICH DAY. Every question asks for a day from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027; any other day answers `not covered`. The
-- notice says weekly payments "are indexed on the anniversary of the entitlement to weekly payments" (lines 21-22, 401-402),
-- and the 1985 Act notice adds "or on the deemed anniversary date which for the purposes of this section is 1 July"
-- (line 22). So the weekly payment questions ask for the day the worker's weekly payments were last indexed, and use the
-- column in force on that day (NOTES.md finding 4).
--
