§ `Victorian workers' compensation amounts from 1 July 2026 -- the injured worker`

§§ `Weekly payments (2013 Act ss 161-166; 1985 Act ss 93A-93CDA)`

@export What is the most I can be paid each week in workers' compensation weekly payments in Victoria (the notice's maximum weekly payment, less what it takes off for my current weekly earnings)?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under: the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013, or, for an older claim, the Accident Compensation Act 1985 (your insurer's decision says which)
      `the day my weekly payments were last indexed` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day your weekly payments were indexed: the anniversary of your entitlement to weekly payments (for a 1985 Act claim, or the deemed anniversary of 1 July); if they have not been indexed yet (your entitlement began less than a year ago, and for a 1985 Act claim no 1 July has passed since), the day your entitlement to weekly payments began; must be from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim; used only for a 1985 Act claim, whose maximum depends on whether it was made before 12 November 1997, before 5 April 2010, or later
      `my entitlement period` IS AN `Entitlement period` @desc Which entitlement period you are in, as the Act defines them: the first, the second, or after the second
      `I have a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a current work capacity (you can do some work, though not your pre-injury work)
      `I have a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a serious injury as the 1985 Act uses the term; used only for a 1985 Act claim made before 12 November 1997
      `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application to keep receiving weekly payments after the second entitlement period, having returned to work, has been approved (2013 Act s 165(1), or 1985 Act s 93CD(1)); used only after the second entitlement period with a current work capacity
      `my current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you now earn each week from work, in Australian dollars (0 if nothing)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most I can be paid each week` `the Act my claim is under` `the day my weekly payments were last indexed` `the day I made my claim` `my entitlement period` `I have a current work capacity` `I have a serious injury` `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved` `my current weekly earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day my weekly payments were last indexed`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `my maximum weekly payment row`
        WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
        WHEN `answered` `the row` THEN `answered` (`the ceiling under` `the row` `in` `the column` `with current weekly earnings of` `my current weekly earnings`)
    WHERE
        `my maximum weekly payment row` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
            WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
                `the 2013 Act maximum weekly payment row for` `my entitlement period` `with capacity` `I have a current work capacity` `approved` `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved`
            WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
                `the 1985 Act maximum weekly payment row for` `my entitlement period` `for` (`the 1985 Act claim band for a claim made on` `the day I made my claim`) `with capacity` `I have a current work capacity` `serious injury` `I have a serious injury` `approved` `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved`

@export How much will my weekly payments be after the notice's maximum (the amount the Act's formula gives me, or the maximum less the deduction for my current earnings, whichever is less)?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under: the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013, or, for an older claim, the Accident Compensation Act 1985
      `the day my weekly payments were last indexed` IS A DATE @desc The most recent day your weekly payments were indexed (the anniversary of your entitlement, or for a 1985 Act claim the deemed anniversary of 1 July), or, if they have not been indexed yet, the day your entitlement to weekly payments began; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim; used only for a 1985 Act claim
      `my entitlement period` IS AN `Entitlement period` @desc Which entitlement period you are in: the first, the second, or after the second
      `I have a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a current work capacity
      `I have a serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a serious injury; used only for a 1985 Act claim made before 12 November 1997
      `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application under 2013 Act s 165(1) or 1985 Act s 93CD(1) has been approved; used only after the second entitlement period
      `my current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you now earn each week from work, in Australian dollars (0 if nothing)
      `the weekly payment the Act's formula gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly payment worked out under the Act before any maximum (the Act's percentage of your pre-injury average weekly earnings, less any deduction it makes for current earnings), in Australian dollars; the Act is not deposited, so this is asked
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my weekly payments after the maximum` `the Act my claim is under` `the day my weekly payments were last indexed` `the day I made my claim` `my entitlement period` `I have a current work capacity` `I have a serious injury` `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved` `my current weekly earnings` `the weekly payment the Act's formula gives me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most I can be paid each week` `the Act my claim is under` `the day my weekly payments were last indexed` `the day I made my claim` `my entitlement period` `I have a current work capacity` `I have a serious injury` `my application to continue weekly payments after returning to work is approved` `my current weekly earnings`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the ceiling` THEN `answered` (`the lesser of` `the weekly payment the Act's formula gives me` `and the ceiling` `the ceiling`)

@export What minimum weekly earnings does the notice set for keeping or getting back my weekly payments after the second entitlement period?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the figure (the Act decides which day counts); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which minimum` IS A `Minimum earnings row` @desc Which of the notice's minimum earnings rows: for continuing weekly payments for an incapacity arising from surgery, or for approval of an application by a worker who has returned to work
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the minimum weekly earnings the notice sets for me` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which minimum` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST (`the 2013 Act minimum earnings for` `which minimum`)) `or` (JUST (`the 1985 Act minimum earnings for` `which minimum`))

-- What "reach" means (at least the figure) is read in wcin-common.l4, not here.
@export Do my current weekly earnings reach the notice's minimum for keeping or getting back my weekly payments?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the answer; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which minimum` IS A `Minimum earnings row` @desc Which of the notice's minimum earnings rows
      `my current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What you now earn each week from work, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`do my current weekly earnings reach the minimum` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which minimum` `my current weekly earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minimum weekly earnings the notice sets for me` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which minimum`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the minimum` THEN `answered` (`weekly earnings of` `my current weekly earnings` `reach the minimum of` `the minimum`)

§§ `Pre-injury average weekly earnings (2013 Act s 153(5), s 544, Schedule 2; 1985 Act s 5A(5), s 100B, Schedule 1A)`

@export What deemed pre-injury average weekly earnings does the notice set for me?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the figure (the Act decides which day counts, such as the day of injury); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which item` IS A `Pre-injury earnings item` @desc Which Schedule item: item 1 where no rate is applicable; item 10 for a full-time student at the completion of a course; item 11 for a full-time school student at the completion of secondary school
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the deemed pre-injury earnings the notice sets for me` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which item` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST (`the 2013 Act Schedule 2 amount for` `which item`)) `or` (JUST (`the 1985 Act Schedule 1A amount for` `which item`))

§§ `Non-economic loss for permanent or psychiatric impairment (2013 Act ss 211-217; 1985 Act s 98C)`

@export What amounts does the notice print for my impairment benefit rating (2013 Act s 211 or s 212; 1985 Act s 98C)?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the figures (the Act decides which day counts); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `my impairment` IS AN `Impairment kind` @desc Whether the rating is for a permanent (physical) impairment or a psychiatric impairment
      `how my rating is described` IS A `Rating description` @desc How your assessment describes the rating: a whole person impairment, a modified whole person impairment, a spinal impairment, or a modified spinal impairment (used only for a 2013 Act claim)
      `my rating in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your impairment benefit rating, or degree of psychiatric impairment, as a percentage (15 for 15%)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Impairment figures`
`the amounts the notice prints for my rating` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `my impairment` `how my rating is described` `my rating in per cent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
            CONSIDER `the 2013 Act impairment band for` `my impairment` `described as` `how my rating is described` `rated at` `my rating in per cent`
            WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
            WHEN `answered` `the band` THEN `answered` (`the 2013 Act impairment figures for` `the band` `in` `the column`)
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
            CONSIDER `the 1985 Act impairment band for` `my impairment` `rated at` `my rating in per cent`
            WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
            WHEN `answered` `the band` THEN `answered` (`the 1985 Act impairment figures for` `the band` `in` `the column`)

@export How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss after the notice's maximum for my impairment band?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount (the Act decides which day counts); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `my impairment` IS AN `Impairment kind` @desc Whether the rating is for a permanent (physical) impairment or a psychiatric impairment
      `how my rating is described` IS A `Rating description` @desc How your assessment describes the rating (used only for a 2013 Act claim)
      `my rating in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your impairment benefit rating, or degree of psychiatric impairment, as a percentage
      `the amount the Act's formula gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc The lump sum the Act's formula gives from the amounts the notice prints for your band, before any maximum, in Australian dollars; the Act is not deposited, so this is asked (not used above 80%, where the notice prints a single amount)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my non-economic loss lump sum after the maximum` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `my impairment` `how my rating is described` `my rating in per cent` `the amount the Act's formula gives me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
            CONSIDER `the 2013 Act impairment band for` `my impairment` `described as` `how my rating is described` `rated at` `my rating in per cent`
            WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
            WHEN `answered` `the band` THEN `the 2013 Act non-economic loss lump sum for` `the band` `in` `the column` `on a formula amount of` `the amount the Act's formula gives me`
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
            CONSIDER `the 1985 Act impairment band for` `my impairment` `rated at` `my rating in per cent`
            WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
            WHEN `answered` `the band` THEN `answered` (`the 1985 Act non-economic loss lump sum for` `the band` `in` `the column` `on a formula amount of` `the amount the Act's formula gives me`)

@export What amounts does the notice print for my further injury (industrial deafness, 2013 Act s 213(1)) or further impairment (2013 Act s 214A), by 'T' and 'P'?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints these rows)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the figures; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which provision` IS A `2013 Act further impairment provision` @desc s 213(1) for a further injury (industrial deafness), or s 214A for a further impairment
      `T in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc 'T' as your assessment states it, as a percentage (the notice uses 'T' and 'P' without defining them)
      `P in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc 'P' as your assessment states it, as a percentage
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Impairment figures`
`the amounts the notice prints for my further impairment` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which provision` `T in per cent` `P in per cent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN `the 2013 Act further impairment figures for` `which provision` `with T` `T in per cent` `and P` `P in per cent` `in` `the column`
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

DECLARE `Other non-economic loss` IS ONE OF
    `the loss of a foetus or of more than one foetus (2013 Act s 214(1))`
    `an impairment resulting from an injury in section 90D (1985 Act s 98C(3B))`

@export What does the notice print for my other non-economic loss: the loss of a foetus (2013 Act s 214(1)), or an impairment from an injury in s 90D (1985 Act s 98C(3B))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `my loss` IS AN `Other non-economic loss` @desc The loss of a foetus or of more than one foetus (a 2013 Act row), or an impairment resulting from an injury in s 90D (a 1985 Act row)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the amount the notice prints for my other non-economic loss` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `my loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my loss`
    WHEN `the loss of a foetus or of more than one foetus (2013 Act s 214(1))` THEN
        `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 214(1) amount`) `or` NOTHING
    WHEN `an impairment resulting from an injury in section 90D (1985 Act s 98C(3B))` THEN
        `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` NOTHING `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 98C(3B) amount`)

@export What is my total non-economic loss after the maximum for more than one injury on the same occasion, or more than one kind of loss from the same injury (2013 Act s 217; 1985 Act s 98C(7), (8))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which limit` IS A `Non-economic loss limit` @desc More than one injury suffered on the same occasion, or more than one kind of non-economic loss for the same injury
      `my total before the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The total non-economic loss compensation for the injuries or kinds of loss, before this maximum, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my total non-economic loss after the limit` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which limit` `my total before the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
            `answered` (`the 2013 Act total non-economic loss after the s 217 maximum for` `which limit` `on a total of` `my total before the limit` `in` `the column`)
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN
            `answered` (`the 1985 Act total non-economic loss after the s 98C(7) or (8) maximum for` `which limit` `on a total of` `my total before the limit` `in` `the column`)

§§ `The no-disadvantage table (2013 Act s 221, Schedule 4) -- only if the no-disadvantage provision applies to you`

@export If the no-disadvantage provision applies to me, what does the Schedule 4 table give for my loss (2013 Act s 221)?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints this table)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `my loss` IS A `Schedule 4 loss` @desc The loss in the Schedule 4 table, in the table's own words
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`what the no-disadvantage table gives for my loss` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `my loss` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST (`the 2013 Act Schedule 4 amount for` `my loss`)) `or` NOTHING

@export What is my total under the no-disadvantage table after the s 221(4) maximum total?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints this table)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `my table total before the maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc The total the Act allows you under the Schedule 4 table for all your losses, before the s 221(4) maximum, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my no-disadvantage total after the maximum` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `my table total before the maximum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN
            `answered` (`the 2013 Act Schedule 4 total after the s 221(4) maximum of` `my table total before the maximum` `in` `the column`)
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

§§ `Medical and like services, and provisional payments (2013 Act ss 224, 229, 243; 1985 Act ss 92D, 99)`

@export What contribution towards the cost of supported accommodation does the notice set for me (2013 Act s 229(4); 1985 Act s 99(15))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`my supported accommodation contribution` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 229(4) contribution`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 99(15) contribution`)

@export What is the most provisional payments can pay for medical and other costs (2013 Act s 243(1)(b); 1985 Act s 92D(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most provisional payments can pay for my medical and other costs` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 243(1)(b) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 92D(1)(b) maximum`)

@export What is the most my family can be paid for counselling, therapy and other support services (2013 Act s 224(1)(b); 1985 Act s 99(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most my family can be paid for counselling and support` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(b) maximum`) `or` (JUST `the 1985 Act s 99(1)(b) maximum`)

-- Asked when the worker has been hospitalised: only then can the row apply.
@export If I was severely injured and taken straight to hospital, what is the most my family can be paid for travel and accommodation to be with me (2013 Act s 224(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints this row)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `I was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were severely injured, as the Act uses the term, and immediately hospitalised following the injury
      `how far my family member lives from the hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc The distance from your family member's residence to the hospital, in kilometres
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most my family can be paid to be with me in hospital` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `I was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` `how far my family member lives from the hospital` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN `the 2013 Act s 224(1)(d) maximum where severely injured and hospitalised` `I was severely injured and immediately hospitalised` `at` `how far my family member lives from the hospital` `in` `the column`
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN `not covered` `the notice prints no row for this under the Act named`

§§ `Dispute resolution costs (2013 Act s 301) -- if you attend a dispute`

@export What is the most I can be paid for my reasonable transport expenses or my loss of income in a dispute (2013 Act s 301(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under (only the 2013 Act notice prints these rows)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the amount; from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `which cost` IS A `Dispute cost` @desc Your reasonable transportation expenses (s 301(3)) or your loss of income (s 301(4)); the notice does not say per what (day, attendance)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most I can be paid for a dispute cost` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `which cost` MEANS
    `the figure under` `the Act my claim is under` `on` `the day I ask about` `from` (JUST (`the 2013 Act s 301 maximum for` `which cost`)) `or` NOTHING

§§ `Damages (2013 Act s 340; 1985 Act ss 134AB, 135A) -- if you sue for damages`

@export What are the threshold and the maximum for my damages for pecuniary loss, or for pain and suffering?
GIVEN `the Act my claim is under` IS A `Governing Act` @desc Which Act your claim is under
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the figures (the Act decides which day counts); from 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2027
      `the 1985 Act section for my damages` IS A `1985 Act damages section` @desc For a 1985 Act claim, which damages section governs your injury, s 134AB or s 135A (the Act decides, by the injury's date); not used for a 2013 Act claim
      `which damages` IS A `Head of damages` @desc Damages for pecuniary loss (loss of earnings and the like), or for pain and suffering
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Damages figures`
`the threshold and maximum for my damages` `the Act my claim is under` `the day I ask about` `the 1985 Act section for my damages` `which damages` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notice column in force on` `the day I ask about`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the column` THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act my claim is under`
        WHEN `the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013` THEN `answered` (`the 2013 Act s 340 figures for` `which damages` `in` `the column`)
        WHEN `the Accident Compensation Act 1985` THEN `answered` (`the 1985 Act damages figures under` `the 1985 Act section for my damages` `for` `which damages` `in` `the column`)
